/**
 * @mainpage Music Composition Core
 *
 * MCC is a portable music-theory library for desktop and embedded targets,
 * built on Foundation. CMake and direct source builds use C++17; Arduino
 * source builds support stock C++11 cores. Its value types are trivially
 * copyable and allocation-free, and it contains no MIDI concepts.
 *
 * @section MCCMainModules Modules
 *
 * - @ref MCC_Pitch "Pitch": `Letter`, `Accidental`, `NoteName` (spelled,
 *   `C#` != `Db`), `PitchClass` (0-11), `ChromaticIndex` and `Pitch`
 *   (scientific pitch notation, middle C is `C4`).
 * - @ref MCC_Interval "Interval": `Interval` (directed diatonic + chromatic
 *   distance, quality and number), inversion, `IntervalBetween()` and
 *   spelling-preserving transposition (`E4 + M3 = G#4`).
 * - @ref MCC_Tuning "Tuning": `Tuning` and `EqualTemperament` frequencies
 *   (`A4 = 440 Hz`); the only module that uses `float`.
 * - @ref MCC_Scale "Scale": spelling-preserving `ScalePattern`, `Scale` and
 *   the reviewed `Scales` catalog.
 * - @ref MCC_Chord "Chord": `ChordPattern`, `Chord`, close-position
 *   inversions and the reviewed `Chords` catalog.
 * - @ref MCC_Key "Key": `KeySignature` and diatonic-mode `Key` spelling.
 * - @ref MCC_Notation "Notation": allocation-free formatting and parsing in
 *   ASCII, UTF-8, UTF-16 and UTF-32.
 * - @ref MCC_Rhythm "Rhythm": exact written `NoteValue` lengths from whole
 *   notes through 256th notes, `Note` as `Pitch + NoteValue`, and written
 *   simple, compound or irregular `Meter` signatures.
 * - @ref MCC_Core "Core": version information.
 *
 * Every rule these types follow is defined in the
 * @ref MCC_Specification "Music-Domain Specification".
 *
 * @section MCCMainDependency Dependency
 *
 * MCC consumes the CMake target `Foundation::Foundation` (Foundation 2.0.0 or
 * a newer 2.x release, built on CPSTL). It uses a local Foundation package when one is
 * available and otherwise fetches the pinned Foundation release from GitHub;
 * see @ref MCC_BuildGuide_Dependency.
 */
